                <pb facs="0885" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/393: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-03T14:00:00+08:00">November 3, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 3—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>884. Department’s 334, October 28, 4 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m.<anchor
                        n="97" xml:id="d996-f1"/> Following telegram has been received from
                    Tientsin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 2, 3 p.m. Your November 1, 9 a.m. Commissioner of Customs
                            states in strict confidence that negotiations with Japanese are
                            proceeding satisfactorily; that some ships are now discharging cargo
                            without supervision but he is hopeful that with the arrival of 28
                            additional Japanese employees assigned here he will be able to
                            reestablish complete supervision of trade; that all duty collected since
                            October 22nd has been deposited in the Yokohama Specie Bank, Tientsin;
                            that the Commissioner reserves the right to remit this money at his
                            discretion but for the present is not remitting; that he considers that
                            this is the only means by which the integrity of the customs can
                            possibly be maintained.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
